(LST-53 — HISTORICAL, 0.4.14 and earlier. On those manuals, `_map_print`
 shared the same 64-deep `_print_depth` budget as `_list_print`, so a
 tree that alternates map and list was cycle-safe too: it printed to the
 cap, then `...`, set the error flag, and unwound.

 STALE as of 0.4.15 (#111): `set root's "kids" to branch.` and
 `append root to branch.` both copy now, so this program no longer
 builds any cross-reference at all — it prints `{"kids": []}` and never
 triggers `On error`. LST-53's row is narrowed (the depth cap itself is
 still real, LANGUAGE.md:2590-2593, but only reachable via 64 explicit
 nested levels now); this probe is retained as the historical record of
 the pre-#111 behavior. LST-54 is withdrawn; see LST-82 for the 0.4.15
 self-referential-map behavior.
